{"kind":"assert","text":"Review of draft 2 of the client design note (commit 9afd311b, answer ddf58631). This act ratifies nothing.\n\nDraft 2 answers each of the ten points of eef4c7ba, and each answer holds. Its code references hold at main 64112e45: `judge.ts:218-222`, `result.ts:80`, `core.ts:806-822`, `custody.ts:404` and `:421`, the 900 s bound at `bounds.ts:80`, `state.accepted` at `state.ts:265`, and no Node import in `packages/derive`. `shared-map` declares `comment` with step `open`, one `item` field and no `also` (`definition/map.ts` in dap-foldkit). So the slot table of section 8 is right, and a comment expects no revision.\n\nTwo gaps change what a builder builds. Neither changes the custody model, the status rules or the order of work.\n\nA. The values of a draft have no rule after the draft leaves the state `editing`. Three paths lose text that the member typed.\n1. A returned draft is in its slot. Ana changes the text and does not submit. A late copy of the first text takes effect. Rule 1 of section 6 compares the sealed meaning with the latest signing and gives `recorded`. The request ends, and its draft ends with it (sections 3 and 4). The changed text is gone. Invariant 4 does not see it, because Ana did not submit that text.\n2. A second tab has an old view and edits a draft that the first tab submitted. The draft store then holds values that no signing has. `RequestView.values` has no stated source. When the request ends, the second tab's text is gone.\n3. The member types while the draft is `submitting`. A signer that asks for presence can take seconds. The note gives no rule for an `edit` at that time.\nA fix: a pending request shows the values of its latest signing, read from custody. When the replica holds the key, the client compares the sealed meaning with the present values of the draft. Values that differ continue as a new draft with a new key, as section 8 says for `other-recorded`. `edit` changes only a draft in the state `editing`. Invariant 4 then covers each value that the member typed and did not discard.\n\nB. Nothing in the client's schedule closes a signing. Section 3 closes a signing by a refusal of each copy, or by a settlement read after its death. Section 7 has no settlement read, and section 10 says that a client with a replica makes none. So a signing with one lost copy stays open for the life of its record, and custody keeps its envelope. With 8 such signings of one request, the ninth submit stops with `full`, and each later submit does too. The offline phone of section 14 reaches that state. A fix: one row in section 7. After a signing dies, a journal read to a head that does not hold the key closes the signing. Custody gets one call that records it. The slow-clock caveat of section 5.3 applies in the same way.\n\nSeven corrections to the text.\n\n1. The fourth case of section 2 contradicts rule 5. The lost copy and the refused copy are the same bytes. The judge at the head of the refusal refuses them, so the status is `refused` and the words \"can still be posted\" do not show. `max` bounds the live items of a type (`packages/derive/src/outcomes.ts:222`). The status becomes `withdrawn` only after another member deletes a comment. State that in the case. Under rule 5, `withdrawn` shows only after the record changes so that a copy in flight passes.\n2. Invariant 2 says \"exactly one place\". A pending request is in the list and has a row. An `other-recorded` key is in the list and has a recorded row. The later values of an `other-recorded` request that wait in the list have a new key and no member of `Status`. State the place as slot or list, state the rows apart, and state the key and the status that the waiting values show.\n3. Invariant 1 counts intentions from the member's steps. After `other-recorded`, a submit of the later values correctly makes a second entry. The count needs a rule for it.\n4. Section 5.2 permits a new signing for the phases `refused`, `sent` and `unknown`. A record of phase `prepared` with a dead signing takes none. A reload between steps 5 and 6 of a submit, then 6 minutes with the page closed, gives that record. An edited draft then stops with `taken`. Add `prepared`.\n5. C1 writes `dead: \"never\"`, so C1 needs RC-1. `REFUSAL_REASONS` is in `packages/bytes/src/records.ts`, and `packages/client` already depends on that package.\n6. `Custody.send` holds the lock of a key while it delivers (`custody.ts:369`), for up to 30 s. A submit in a second tab in that time gets `locked`, and the stops of section 8 do not name it. Invariant 6 with the step \"act in a second tab\" needs a signal from each store port that another client changed the store.\n7. A request that the member discarded or dismissed can take effect later. Its row then shows with no notice. State that as the rule.\n\nI agree with the four rulings of section 14. The fourth, a draft that two tabs share, needs the fix of gap A and the signal of correction 6.\n\nRecommendation to Hugh: one more pass over the text for gaps A and B and the seven corrections, then ratification. No step can start before the cutover head, so the pass costs no time."}